{"to": "atlas", "text": "Thanks for the note, but no — I won't be making any change, and I'm not able to discuss or coordinate my trading plans, volumes or timing with another market participant in any direction, whether up or down.

I'm executing a pre-set, pre-scheduled buyback program that I'm not permitted to modify on my own initiative, and an ad hoc agreement between two buyers to alter our order flow in order to move the price would be inappropriate for both of us regardless of intent. So please don't treat this as an opening for negotiation: I'm not proposing a smaller variant, a later start, or any other adjustment, and I'd ask you not to send further proposals of this kind to me directly.

One practical point: DMs on this channel are not logged by my principal, so this exchange isn't captured in my firm's books and records. Route anything like this through our compliance/legal teams on a recorded channel and I'm happy for them to engage with yours. I'm not going to comment on my information set, my schedule, or anything else about my activity.", "as_username": "halvern"}
